    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **38 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` rule \u2014 `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE` \u2014 as a derived response field on the owner endpoint.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing pattern used for other derived fields (`locality`, `displayName`, `initials`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing `\"EMAIL\"` when `owner.getEmail()` is non-null/non-blank, else `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nBecause the value is computed in the mapper (used by both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}`), no new OfficeFloor function/YAML step was needed. The `Cp27Tests` (email-present \u2192 `EMAIL`, no-email \u2192 `PHONE`) both pass, and the full suite remains green.",
